        <div class="learning-points">
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <strong>A4.1.1</strong> — Definitions of Artificial Intelligence (Narrow vs. General) and Machine Learning. Characteristics of Supervised, Unsupervised, Reinforcement, Deep Learning, and Transfer Learning.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>A4.1.1</strong> — Applications: Medical imaging diagnostics, NLP, market basket analysis, robotics navigation, and sentiment analysis.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>A4.1.2</strong> — Hardware deployment: From standard laptops to advanced infrastructure (GPUs, TPUs, ASICs, FPGAs, Edge devices, and Cloud-based platforms).
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>A4.4.1</strong> — Ethical implications: Accountability, algorithmic fairness, bias in training data, consent, and societal impact.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>A4.4.2</strong> — Emerging integration: Pervasive AI, Quantum computing, AR, and VR.
                </li>
            </ul>
