    <!-- Watch Out For -->
    <section class="exam-section" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fff3cd 0%, #ffe5a0 100%); border-left-color: #ffc107;">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation section-icon" style="color: #856404;"></i> Common Misconceptions</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>AI "Understanding":</strong> Students often believe AI has human-like intent or consciousness, rather than being a statistical engine finding generalizations in data.</li>
            <li><strong>General AI:</strong> Believing that "Strong AI" (human-level across all domains) is currently available technology (Textbook Clarification: only Narrow AI is available).</li>
            <li><strong>Data Objectivity:</strong> The belief that data is inherently neutral, ignoring that human bias is frequently encoded into training sets.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Big Ideas -->
    <section class="content-section" style="border-top-color: var(--accent-color);">
